# What never gets uploaded to Vercel.
#
# This exists because `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory, not the
# git tree. Everything in .gitignore is still sitting on disk — including
# samples/*_raw.txt, which are real bank SMS with real account numbers, and
# api/.env, which holds the ingest secret. Keeping them out of git is not the
# same as keeping them off a build server, and only this file does the second.
#
# The service config cannot do this job: `root: "api/"` scopes the BUILD, and
# `excludeFiles` is not a valid key in the `services` model at all. Exclusion
# from the upload happens here or nowhere.

# Real personal data
samples/
sms.txt
*.private.txt

# Secrets. Vercel takes environment variables from project settings; a .env
# file reaching the build is only ever a leak.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not part of either service's build
tests/
tools/
*.md
!README.md

# Local build and dependency output
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
node_modules/
.next/
